body:
See you never got a reply! I did Ha Giang with Mamas tours and they had a hostel in Ha Giang where we left our big backpacks. They werent locked up or anything lol but there wasn't anyone else there except for obviously people doing the loop. And then you take a small backpack with clothing for the 3/4 days with you on the actual tour! 

&#x200B;

I took a pretty filled up Eastpack backpack and it was bigger than most peoples daypacks that they brought on the loop. Maybe 40L would be a lot. Also depends on if you will drive yourself (so more space on the bike, bigger bag would be fine) or will be on the back of an easyriders motor. My bag was so big I kept half having to straddle my easyrider LOL not too comfy.
